      "message": "The analysis completed, so a quantity may be reported as measured - but only once a typed measurement envelope carries it. A number parsed out of the raw file by hand is not one: nothing in the result contract binds it to this run. This envelope has been retained at /evidence/sim/ngspice-op/simulate.result.json. The retained raw declares the vectors v(vin), v(vdd), v(vout), i(v2), i(v1); an operating point has no axis. Continue with: openada extract --simulation /evidence/sim/ngspice-op/simulate.result.json --artifact /evidence/sim/ngspice-op/inverter-op/inverter-op.raw --selection /evidence/sim/ngspice-op/simulate.selection.json, then `openada measure` on the series it returns; its kinds are sample_at, minimum, maximum, mean, rms, crossing, rise_time, fall_time and settling_time, each reading ONE named signal. A ratio of two signals is not among them - for a gain, a differential gain or a driving-point impedance, run an AC analysis and use `openada transfer`. `openada spectral` covers snr, sinad, thd and sfdr on a coherent single tone."
